    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "17 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-03 23:13:00 CDT Expires: 2025-09-04 00:00:00 CDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Target Area: Gibson; Pike At 1112 PM CDT/1212 AM EDT/, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near Patoka, or 8 miles northeast of Princeton, moving east at 45 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects.\nLocations impacted include... Princeton, Oakland City, Petersburg, Winslow, Patoka, and Hazleton.\nThis includes Interstate 69 in Indiana between Mile Markers 34 and 52.",
